  "body": "My mailto: handler, set via registerProtocolHandler() is Gmail. Today [I learned](https://twitter.com/ericlaw/status/1228011652001472512) that if I click on a mailto: handler in a subframe, that subframe will attempt to navigate to GMail, which will fail for any number of reasons:\r\n\r\n  1. Tracking Prevention deems this a privacy violation\r\n  2. The subframe will fail to load due to a restrictive Frame-Ancestors policy forbidding framing\r\n  3. SameSite cookies will not be sent because the content is in a cross-origin parent\r\n\r\nNow, the simple answer is that every custom scheme handler link written by a web developer should have a `target=\"_top\"`  or `target=_blank` attribute, but this forces web authors to be aware of this problem.\r\n\r\nIf we want web-based custom scheme handlers to be able to effectively replace native custom scheme handlers, perhaps we should remove this footgun by specifying that invocation of custom scheme handlers should act as if target=_top by default, unless specified otherwise?\r\n\r\n\r\n",
